{#- Monochrome link glyphs.

    Inline SVG filled with currentColor, so each glyph takes its link's colour
    and follows it through hover with no rule of its own.

    Sources: Google Scholar and ORCID are the official simple-icons paths;
    LinkedIn and GitHub are Bootstrap Icons (simple-icons dropped LinkedIn over
    trademark); Twitter is the bird SVG in Misc/Logos_for_website, viewBox
    tightened to its measured bbox (50 68.7 200 162.5) so it fills the box like
    the others; IDEAS/EconPapers is a Bootstrap bulb, standing in for the IDEAS
    lightbulb mark, which is a raster and cannot be traced reliably.

    UNU-WIDER and RAND are square marks with their lettering knocked out, built
    with an SVG mask so the hole is genuinely transparent and the tile takes
    currentColor. UNU uses the real wordmark paths from the supplied logo (fitted
    to the box from its measured bbox, 188.41 6.56 313.98 113.77); RAND's R is
    type, which is why both live inline — an external SVG used as a mask cannot
    reach the page's fonts. -#}

